    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2NswrB4bSkiQMXwFuMJXv4Z)_\n\n## Cause\n`sp-citations` sets `(note . ,sp-citar-note)` in `citar-templates`, but `sp-citar-note` (in `sp-globals`) defaulted to `nil`. Citar then has no `note` template and signals `No template for \"note\"` when the note indicator runs, which happens in `jit-lock` during redisplay.\n\n## Fix\n`sp-citar-note` now defaults to citar's own string, `\"Notes on ${author editor:%etal}, ${title}\"`, with `:type 'string`. Literate doc and CHANGELOG updated.\n\n## Not tested\nNothing was run in Emacs (none in the container). If you customized `sp-citar-note` to nil, set it to a string.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAdt8amQYKFvPPhzbg)_",
